# Pool state: config is per-machine, backups and sessions are local history.
# Registered API specs are the one exception -- a spec is a fact about an
# external service, not per-machine state, so it travels with the repo
# instead of needing `openapi.py --add` re-run (and the real API re-fetched)
# on every new box. `.swarm/*` (not `.swarm/`) so git still recurses into
# the directory far enough for the negation below to take effect.
.swarm/*
!.swarm/specs/
!.swarm/specs/**
config.local.json
config_*.json

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.bak-*

# Measurement output from one-off experiments.
critic_eval_*.json
plan_demo.json
.commitmsg

# Deliberately NOT listing generated packages here any more.
#
# This file used to name each one as it appeared -- graphkit/, textkit/,
# dupfinder.py, and so on -- and the list grew for months. Two things went
# wrong with that. Debris became invisible: `git status` stayed clean while
# ten abandoned packages and a dozen pygame files accumulated at the root,
# until a `for t in *_test.py` loop ran one of them and hung the terminal.
# And the same pattern caught real work by accident: twelve hand-written
# machinery tests were ignored alongside the junk, including the four AGENTS.md
# cites by name, so a fresh clone had no test suite at all.
#
# Untracked debris showing up in `git status` is the feature. Delete it or
# commit it, but see it.

# never commit credentials
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
credentials
